=====================================================================
Problems Caused Through Network Drivers.
---------------------------------------------------------------------

The PALASM 4 menu system processes many commands by paging in and out and
executing other programs supplied in the 'EXE' subdirectory. The following
is a list of known system configurations that may cause menu operation
failures:

1.      Using PALASM 4 across networks not supported
2.      Network drivers are loaded in low-memory (ie address < 640K)

See below for more detailed explanations.

---------------------------------------------------------------------
1.      Using PALASM 4 across networks not supported
---------------------------------------------------------------------
No testing has been done to vailidate using the PALASM 4 software across PC
networks.  We do not currently recommend using the software in this manner.

---------------------------------------------------------------------
2.      Network drivers are loaded in low-memory (ie address < 640K)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
Loading Network drivers (eg, PC-NFS, 3COM, NOVEL, RAF etc. drivers in
your CONFIG.SYS file) is known to cause sporadic failures in the PALASM 4
memory system when loaded in low memory. It is not yet known whether
these are problems cause by interference between the software or purely
because they reduce the availability of low-end memory. If you are
having problems try loading these drivers into high memory (ie. address
> 640K)

Note: You do not need to be using the network to potentially see
      problems through loaded network drivers.

